     "explanation": "Myelin enables fast saltatory conduction by insulating the axon so the signal can jump node to node. When MS strips the myelin away, current leaks out across the bare membrane instead of being conserved between nodes. Conduction slows dramatically or fails entirely, producing MS symptoms. The resting potential, channel gating, and the Na+/K+ pump are not what demyelination directly removes — it is the insulation that is lost.",
