    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Run the Transduction Chain for Each Sense",
     "content": "Every sense follows the same logic: physical energy → receptor → transduction → pathway → cortex. Practice filling in the chain for each.\n\nFor each sense, name: (1) the physical stimulus, (2) the receptor, (3) the relay (usually the thalamus), and (4) the cortical destination.\n\n• **Vision:** light → rods/cones in retina → thalamus (LGN) → occipital cortex\n• **Hearing:** air pressure waves → hair cells in cochlea → thalamus → temporal (auditory) cortex\n• **Touch:** mechanical pressure → skin receptors → thalamus → parietal (somatosensory) cortex\n• **Smell:** odor molecules → olfactory receptors → (bypasses thalamus!) → limbic/cortex directly\n\nCover the answers and rebuild each chain from memory. Note the odd one out: smell skips the thalamus. Mastering this common template lets you reason about any sensory system, even ones you've never studied.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE: TRANSDUCTION</text>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Stimulus to cortex</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"170\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.13)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Vision</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Light to retina</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Thalamus to occipital cortex</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"322\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.13)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Hearing</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Waves to cochlea</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Thalamus to temporal cortex</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"474\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.13)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"522\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Touch</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"562\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Pressure to skin</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"592\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Thalamus to parietal cortex</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"626\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.13)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"674\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Smell</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"714\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Odor to olfactory receptors</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"744\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Skips thalamus!</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "Build each sensory chain"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Catch Your Brain Filling In the Gaps",
     "content": "Perception is construction, and you can catch your brain doing it. Try these classic demonstrations and explain each one neurally.\n\n1. **The blind spot:** Close your left eye, stare at a dot with your right, and move a pen sideways. It vanishes where the optic nerve exits the retina — yet you don't see a hole, because the brain *fills it in*.\n2. **Adaptation:** Rest your hand in warm water, then cold, then lukewarm with the other hand. The same lukewarm water feels different to each hand — perception is relative, not absolute.\n3. **The McGurk effect:** Seeing lips say 'ga' while hearing 'ba' makes you perceive 'da.' Vision rewrites hearing — proof the brain integrates senses.\n4. **Gestalt grouping:** Three dots are seen as a triangle. The brain imposes wholes on parts.\n\nFor each, explain WHY: the brain prioritizes a coherent best-guess model over raw input. Note how each illusion exposes the construction.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE: PERCEPTION TRICKS</text>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Catch the brain constructing</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"170\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.13)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"238\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">1</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Blind spot</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"254\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Brain fills the missing hole</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"298\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.13)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"366\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">2</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Temperature adaptation</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"382\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Perception is relative</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"426\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.13)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"494\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">3</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"476\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">McGurk effect</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Vision rewrites hearing</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"554\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.13)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"622\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">4</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"604\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Gestalt grouping</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"638\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Wholes imposed on parts</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "Expose the construction at work"
     }
    }
