    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Map Your Own Stress Response",
     "content": "Use the neuroscience of stress to understand and manage your own. Walk through a recent stressful moment and trace the biology.\n\n1. **Identify the trigger** — what activated your amygdala? Was it a real threat (high road) or a false alarm (low road overreacting)?\n2. **Notice the fight-or-flight signs** — racing heart, tense muscles, shallow breath. That's your sympathetic nervous system and adrenaline.\n3. **Recognize the cortisol phase** — the lingering tension, racing thoughts, trouble sleeping. That's the HPA axis and cortisol.\n4. **Engage the high road** — consciously reappraise the threat. Asking 'is this really dangerous?' recruits the prefrontal cortex to calm the amygdala.\n5. **Apply a cortisol off-switch** — slow breathing, exercise, social connection (oxytocin!), and sleep all dampen the stress response.\n\nThe goal: recognize which circuit is firing and use your prefrontal cortex to regulate it. Knowing the biology gives you leverage over it.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE: MAP YOUR STRESS</text>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Use the biology</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"170\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.13)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"238\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">1</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Find the trigger</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"254\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Amygdala: real or false alarm?</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"298\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.13)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"366\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">2</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Notice fight-or-flight</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"382\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Sympathetic + adrenaline</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"426\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.13)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"494\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">3</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"476\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Recognize cortisol</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">The HPA lingering phase</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"554\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.13)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"622\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">4</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"604\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Engage the high road</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"638\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Prefrontal reappraisal</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"682\" width=\"860\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"165\" y=\"750\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">5</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"732\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Apply the off-switch</text>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"766\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Breath, exercise, connection</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "Turn stress science into self-control"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Reframe a Habit Through the Reward Circuit",
     "content": "Habits and cravings are reward-circuit phenomena. Use the dopamine framework to understand and reshape one of your own habits.\n\n1. **Pick a habit** — scrolling your phone, snacking, a morning coffee. Anything pulled by craving.\n2. **Find the cue** — what triggers it? (Boredom, a notification, a time of day.) Cues become linked to dopamine through learning.\n3. **Identify the reward** — what does the dopamine surge reinforce? Often it's relief or novelty, not deep pleasure (recall: dopamine is wanting, not liking).\n4. **Predict the prediction error** — the habit feels most compelling when the reward is *unpredictable* (variable rewards, like social media likes, drive the strongest dopamine — the same principle as slot machines).\n5. **Re-engineer it** — to weaken a habit, make the cue invisible or the reward predictable/boring. To build a good habit, pair a clear cue with an immediate, satisfying reward.\n\nApply this to one habit today. You're using the same circuitry that addiction exploits — but deliberately, in your favor.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE: HABIT REFRAME</text>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Use the reward circuit</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"170\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.13)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Find the cue</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What triggers the craving?</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Cues link to dopamine</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"322\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.13)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Name the reward</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Often relief or novelty</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Wanting, not liking</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"474\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.13)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"522\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Spot variable rewards</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"562\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Unpredictable = strongest pull</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"592\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">The slot-machine effect</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"626\" width=\"860\" height=\"130\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.13)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"674\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Re-engineer it</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"714\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Change cue and reward</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"744\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Use the circuit on purpose</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "Reshape a habit with dopamine logic"
     }
    }
