     "explanation": "Catching a ball integrates many systems: the visual cortex and dorsal stream see and track it (Lesson 6), the cerebellum predicts the trajectory and times the reach (Lessons 4, 7), and the motor cortex with the basal ganglia commands and releases the movement (Lesson 7). No single region acts alone — the hallmark of the integrated brain. The medulla controls autonomic functions, not voluntary movement.",
